msgid ""
"\n"
"Session Support for IPA\n"
"John Dennis <jdennis@redhat.com>\n"
"\n"
"Goals\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Provide per-user session data caching which persists between\n"
"requests. Desired features are:\n"
"\n"
"* Integrates cleanly with minimum impact on existing infrastructure.\n"
"\n"
"* Provides maximum security balanced against real-world performance\n"
"  demands.\n"
"\n"
"* Sessions must be able to be revoked (flushed).\n"
"\n"
"* Should be flexible and easy to use for developers.\n"
"\n"
"* Should leverage existing technology and code to the maximum extent\n"
"  possible to avoid re-invention, excessive implementation time and to\n"
"  benefit from robustness in field proven components commonly shared\n"
"  in the open source community.\n"
"\n"
"* Must support multiple independent processes which share session\n"
"  data.\n"
"\n"
"* System must function correctly if session data is available or not.\n"
"\n"
"* Must be high performance.\n"
"\n"
"* Should not be tied to specific web servers or browsers. Should\n"
"  integrate with our chosen WSGI model.\n"
"\n"
"Issues\n"
"======\n"
"\n"
"Cookies\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"Most session implementations are based on the use of cookies. Cookies\n"
"have some inherent problems.\n"
"\n"
"* User has the option to disable cookies.\n"
"\n"
"* User stored cookie data is not secure. Can be mitigated by setting\n"
"  flags indicating the cookie is only to be used with SSL secured HTTP\n"
"  connections to specific web resources and setting the cookie to\n"
"  expire at session termination. Most modern browsers enforce these.\n"
"\n"
"Where to store session data?\n"
"----------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Session data may be stored on either on the client or on the\n"
"server. Storing session data on the client addresses the problem of\n"
"session data availability when requests are serviced by independent web\n"
"servers because the session data travels with the request. However\n"
"there are data size limitations. Storing session data on the client\n"
"also exposes sensitive data but this can be mitigated by encrypting\n"
"the session data such that only the server can decrypt it.\n"
"\n"
"The more conventional approach is to bind session data to a unique\n"
"name, the session ID. The session ID is transmitted to the client and\n"
"the session data is paired with the session ID on the server in a\n"
"associative data store. The session data is retrieved by the server\n"
"using the session ID when the receiving the request. This eliminates\n"
"exposing sensitive session data on the client along with limitations\n"
"on data size. It however introduces the issue of session data\n"
"availability when requests are serviced by more than one server\n"
"process.\n"
"\n"
"Multi-process session data availability\n"
"---------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Apache (and other web servers) fork child processes to handle requests\n"
"in parallel. Also web servers may be deployed in a farm where requests\n"
"are load balanced in round robin fashion across different nodes. In\n"
"both cases session data cannot be stored in the memory of a server\n"
"process because it is not available to other processes, either sibling\n"
"children of a master server process or server processes on distinct\n"
"nodes.\n"
"\n"
"Typically this is addressed by storing session data in a SQL\n"
"database. When a request is received by a server process containing a\n"
"session ID in it's cookie data the session ID is used to perform a SQL\n"
"query and the resulting data is then attached to the request as it\n"
"proceeds through the request processing pipeline. This of course\n"
"introduces coherency issues.\n"
"\n"
"For IPA the introduction of a SQL database dependency is undesired and\n"
"should be avoided.\n"
"\n"
"Session data may also be shared by independent processes by storing\n"
"the session data in files.\n"
"\n"
"An alternative solution which has gained considerable popularity\n"
"recently is the use of a fast memory based caching server. Data is\n"
"stored in a single process memory and may be queried and set via a\n"
"light weight protocol using standard socket mechanisms, memcached is\n"
"one example. A typical use is to optimize SQL queries by storing a SQL\n"
"result in shared memory cache avoiding the more expensive SQL\n"
"operation. But the memory cache has distinct advantages in non-SQL\n"
"situations as well.\n"
"\n"
"Possible implementations for use by IPA\n"
"=======================================\n"
"\n"
"Apache Sessions\n"
"---------------\n"
"\n"
"Apache has 2.3 has implemented session support via these modules:\n"
"\n"
"  mod_session\n"
"    Overarching session support based on cookies.\n"
"\n"
"    See: http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.3/mod/mod_session.html\n"
"\n"
"  mod_session_cookie\n"
"    Stores session data in the client.\n"
"\n"
"    See: http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.3/mod/mod_session_cookie.html\n"
"\n"
"  mod_session_crypto\n"
"    Encrypts session data for security. Encryption key is shared\n"
"    configuration parameter visible to all Apache processes and is\n"
"    stored in a configuration file.\n"
"\n"
"    See: http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.3/mod/mod_session_crypto.html\n"
"\n"
"  mod_session_dbd\n"
"    Stores session data in a SQL database permitting multiple\n"
"    processes to access and share the same session data.\n"
"\n"
"    See: http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.3/mod/mod_session_dbd.html\n"
"\n"
"Issues with Apache sessions\n"
"~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"\n"
"Although Apache has implemented generic session support and Apache is\n"
"our web server of preference it nonetheless introduces issues for IPA.\n"
"\n"
"  * Session support is only available in httpd >= 2.3 which at the\n"
"    time of this writing is currently only available as a Beta release\n"
"    from upstream. We currently only ship httpd 2.2, the same is true\n"
"    for other distributions.\n"
"\n"
"  * We could package and ship the sessions modules as a temporary\n"
"    package in httpd 2.2 environments. But this has the following\n"
"    consequences:\n"
"\n"
"      - The code has to be backported. the module API has changed\n"
"        slightly between httpd 2.2 and 2.3. The backporting is not\n"
"        terribly difficult and a proof of concept has been\n"
"        implemented.\n"
"\n"
"      - We would then be on the hook to package and maintain a special\n"
"        case Apache package. This is maintenance burden as well as a\n"
"        distribution packaging burden. Both of which would be best\n"
"        avoided if possible.\n"
"\n"
"  * The design of the Apache session modules is such that they can\n"
"    only be manipulated by other Apache modules. The ability of\n"
"    consumers of the session data to control the session data is\n"
"    simplistic, constrained and static during the period the request\n"
"    is processed. Request handlers which are not native Apache modules\n"
"    (e.g. IPA via WSGI) can only examine the session data\n"
"    via request headers and reset it in response headers.\n"
"\n"
"  * Shared session data is available exclusively via SQL.\n"
"\n"
"However using the 2.3 Apache session modules would give us robust\n"
"session support implemented in C based on standardized Apache\n"
"interfaces which are widely used.\n"
"\n"
"Python Web Frameworks\n"
"---------------------\n"
"\n"
"Virtually every Python web framework supports cookie based sessions,\n"
"e.g. Django, Twisted, Zope, Turbogears etc. Early on in IPA we decided\n"
"to avoid the use of these frameworks. Trying to pull in just one part\n"
"of these frameworks just to get session support would be problematic\n"
"because the code does not function outside it's framework.\n"
"\n"
"IPA implemented sessions\n"
"------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Originally it was believed the path of least effort was to utilize\n"
"existing session support, most likely what would be provided by\n"
"Apache. However there are enough basic modular components available in\n"
"native Python and other standard packages it should be possible to\n"
"provide session support meeting the aforementioned goals with a modest\n"
"implementation effort. Because we're leveraging existing components\n"
"the implementation difficulties are subsumed by other components which\n"
"have already been field proven and have community support. This is a\n"
"smart strategy.\n"
"\n"
"Proposed Solution\n"
"=================\n"
"\n"
"Our interface to the web server is via WSGI which invokes a callback\n"
"per request passing us an environmental context for the request. For\n"
"this discussion we'll name the WSGI callback \"application()\", a\n"
"conventional name in WSGI parlance.\n"
"\n"
"Shared session data will be handled by memcached. We will create one\n"
"instance of memcached on each server node dedicated to IPA\n"
"exclusively. Communication with memcached will be via a UNIX socket\n"
"located in the file system under /var/run/ipa_memcached. It will be\n"
"protected by file permissions and optionally SELinux policy.\n"
"\n"
"In application() we examine the request cookies and if there is an IPA\n"
"session cookie with a session ID we retrieve the session data from our\n"
"memcached instance.\n"
"\n"
"The session data will be a Python dict. IPA components will read or\n"
"write their session information by using a pre-agreed upon name\n"
"(e.g. key) in the dict. This is a very flexible system and consistent\n"
"with how we pass data in most parts of IPA.\n"
"\n"
"If the session data is not available an empty session data dict will\n"
"be created.\n"
"\n"
"How does this session data travel with the request in the IPA\n"
"pipeline? In IPA we use the HTTP request/response to implement RPC. In\n"
"application() we convert the request into a procedure call passing it\n"
"arguments derived from the HTTP request. The passed parameters are\n"
"specific to the RPC method being invoked. The context the RPC call is\n"
"executing in is not passed as an RPC parameter.\n"
"\n"
"How would the contextual information such as session data be bound to\n"
"the request and hence the RPC call?\n"
"\n"
"In IPA when a RPC invocation is being prepared from a request we\n"
"recognize this will only ever be processed serially by one Python\n"
"thread. A thread local dict called \"context\" is allocated for each\n"
"thread. The context dict is cleared in between requests (e.g. RPC method\n"
"invocations). The per-thread context dict is populated during the\n"
"lifetime of the request and is used as a global data structure unique to\n"
"the request that various IPA component can read from and write to with\n"
"the assurance the data is unique to the current request and/or method\n"
"call.\n"
"\n"
"The session data dict will be written into the context dict under the\n"
"session key before the RPC method begins execution. Thus session data\n"
"can be read and written by any IPA component by accessing\n"
"``context.session``.\n"
"\n"
"When the RPC method finishes execution the session data bound to the\n"
"request/method is retrieved from the context and written back to the\n"
"memcached instance. The session ID is set in the response sent back to\n"
"the client in the ``Set-Cookie`` header along with the flags\n"
"controlling it's usage.\n"
"\n"
"Issues and details\n"
"------------------\n"
"\n"
"IPA code cannot depend on session data being present, however it\n"
"should always update session data with the hope it will be available\n"
"in the future. Session data may not be available because:\n"
"\n"
"  * This is the first request from the user and no session data has\n"
"    been created yet.\n"
"\n"
"  * The user may have cookies disabled.\n"
"\n"
"  * The session data may have been flushed. memcached operates with\n"
"    a fixed memory allocation and will flush entries on a LRU basis,\n"
"    like with any cache there is no guarantee of persistence.\n"
"\n"
"    Also we may have have deliberately expired or deleted session\n"
"    data, see below.\n"
"\n"
"Cookie manipulation is done via the standard Python Cookie module.\n"
"\n"
"Session cookies will be set to only persist as long as the browser has\n"
"the session open. They will be tagged so the browser only returns\n"
"the session ID on SSL secured HTTP requests. They will not be visible\n"
"to Javascript in the browser.\n"
"\n"
"Session ID's will be created by using 48 bits of random data and\n"
"converted to 12 hexadecimal digits. Newly generated session ID's will\n"
"be checked for prior existence to handle the unlikely case the random\n"
"number repeats.\n"
"\n"
"memcached will have significantly higher performance than a SQL or file\n"
"based storage solution. Communication is effectively though a pipe\n"
"(UNIX socket) using a very simple protocol and the data is held\n"
"entirely in process memory. memcached also scales easily, it is easy\n"
"to add more memcached processes and distribute the load across them.\n"
"At this point in time we don't anticipate the need for this.\n"
"\n"
"A very nice feature of the Python memcached module is that when a data\n"
"item is written to the cache it is done with standard Python pickling\n"
"(pickling is a standard Python mechanism to marshal and unmarshal\n"
"Python objects). We adopt the convention the object written to cache\n"
"will be a dict to meet our internal data handling conventions. The\n"
"pickling code will recursively handle nested objects in the dict. Thus\n"
"we gain a lot of flexibility using standard Python data structures to\n"
"store and retrieve our session data without having to author and debug\n"
"code to marshal and unmarshal the data if some other storage mechanism\n"
"had been used. This is a significant implementation win. Of course\n"
"some common sense limitations need to observed when deciding on what\n"
"is written to the session cache keeping in mind the data is shared\n"
"between processes and it should not be excessively large (a\n"
"configurable option)\n"
"\n"
"We can set an expiration on memcached entries. We may elect to do that\n"
"to force session data to be refreshed periodically. For example we may\n"
"wish the client to present fresh credentials on a periodic basis even\n"
"if the cached credentials are otherwise within their validity period.\n"
"\n"
"We can explicitly delete session data if for some reason we believe it\n"
"is stale, invalid or compromised.\n"
"\n"
"memcached also gives us certain facilities to prevent race conditions\n"
"between different processes utilizing the cache. For example you can\n"
"check of the entry has been modified since you last read it or use CAS\n"
"(Check And Set) semantics. What has to be protected in terms of cache\n"
"coherency will likely have to be determined as the session support is\n"
"utilized and different data items are added to the cache. This is very\n"
"much data and context specific. Fortunately memcached operations are\n"
"atomic.\n"
"\n"
"Controlling the memcached process\n"
"---------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"We need a mechanism to start the memcached process and secure it so\n"
"that only IPA components can access it.\n"
"\n"
"Although memcached ships with both an initscript and systemd unit\n"
"files those are for generic instances. We want a memcached instance\n"
"dedicated exclusively to IPA usage. To accomplish this we would install\n"
"a systemd unit file or an SysV initscript to control the IPA specific\n"
"memcached service. ipactl would be extended to know about this\n"
"additional service. systemd's cgroup facility would give us additional\n"
"mechanisms to integrate the IPA memcached service within a larger IPA\n"
"process group.\n"
"\n"
"Protecting the memcached data would be done via file permissions (and\n"
"optionally SELinux policy) on the UNIX domain socket. Although recent\n"
"implementations of memcached support authentication via SASL this\n"
"introduces a performance and complexity burden not warranted when\n"
"cached is dedicated to our exclusive use and access controlled by OS\n"
"mechanisms.\n"
"\n"
"Conventionally daemons are protected by assigning a system uid and/or\n"
"gid to the daemon. A daemon launched by root will drop it's privileges\n"
"by assuming the effective uid:gid assigned to it. File system access\n"
"is controlled by the OS via the effective identity and SELinux policy\n"
"can be crafted based on the identity. Thus the memcached UNIX socket\n"
"would be protected by having it owned by a specific system user and/or\n"
"membership in a restricted system group (discounting for the moment\n"
"SELinux).\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately we currently do not have an IPA system uid whose\n"
"identity our processes operate under nor do we have an IPA system\n"
"group. IPA does manage a collection of related processes (daemons) and\n"
"historically each has been assigned their own uid. When these\n"
"unrelated processes communicate they mutually authenticate via other\n"
"mechanisms. We do not have much of a history of using shared file\n"
"system objects across identities. When file objects are created they\n"
"are typically assigned the identity of daemon needing to access the\n"
"object and are not accessed by other daemons, or they carry root\n"
"identity.\n"
"\n"
"When our WSGI application runs in Apache it is run as a WSGI\n"
"daemon. This means when Apache starts up it forks off WSGI processes\n"
"for us and we are independent of other Apache processes. When WSGI is\n"
"run in this mode there is the ability to set the uid:gid of the WSGI\n"
"process hosting us, however we currently do not take advantage of this\n"
"option. WSGI can be run in other modes as well, only in daemon mode\n"
"can the uid:gid be independently set from the rest of Apache. All\n"
"processes started by Apache can be set to a common uid:gid specified\n"
"in the global Apache configuration, by default it's\n"
"apache:apache. Thus when our IPA code executes it is running as\n"
"apache:apache.\n"
"\n"
"To protect our memcached UNIX socket we can do one of two things:\n"
"\n"
"1. Assign it's uid:gid as apache:apache. This would limit access to\n"
"   our cache only to processes running under httpd. It's somewhat\n"
"   restricted but far from ideal. Any code running in the web server\n"
"   could potentially access our cache. It's difficult to control what the\n"
"   web server runs and admins may not understand the consequences of\n"
"   configuring httpd to serve other things besides IPA.\n"
"\n"
"2. Create an IPA specific uid:gid, for example ipa:ipa. We then configure\n"
"   our WSGI application to run as the ipa:ipa user and group. We also\n"
"   configure our memcached instance to run as the ipa:ipa user and\n"
"   group. In this configuration we are now fully protected, only our WSGI\n"
"   code can read & write to our memcached UNIX socket.\n"
"\n"
"However there may be unforeseen issues by converting our code to run as\n"
"something other than apache:apache. This would require some\n"
"investigation and testing.\n"
"\n"
"IPA is dependent on other system daemons, specifically Directory\n"
"Server (ds) and Certificate Server (cs). Currently we configure ds to\n"
"run under the dirsrv:dirsrv user and group, an identity of our\n"
"creation. We allow cs to default to it's pkiuser:pkiuser user and\n"
"group. Should these other cooperating daemons also run under the\n"
"common ipa:ipa user and group identities? At first blush there would\n"
"seem to be an advantage to coalescing all process identities under a\n"
"common IPA user and group identity. However these other processes do\n"
"not depend on user and group permissions when working with external\n"
"agents, processes, etc. Rather they are designed to be stand-alone\n"
"network services which authenticate their clients via other\n"
"mechanisms. They do depend on user and group permission to manage\n"
"their own file system objects. If somehow the ipa user and/or group\n"
"were compromised or malicious code somehow executed under the ipa\n"
"identity there would be an advantage in having the cooperating\n"
"processes cordoned off under their own identities providing one extra\n"
"layer of protection. (Note, these cooperating daemons may not even be\n"
"co-located on the same node in which case the issue is moot)\n"
"\n"
"The UNIX socket behavior (ldapi) with Directory Server is as follows:\n"
"\n"
"  * The socket ownership is: root:root\n"
"\n"
"  * The socket permissions are: 0666\n"
"\n"
"  * When connecting via ldapi you must authenticate as you would\n"
"    normally with a TCP socket, except ...\n"
"\n"
"  * If autobind is enabled and the uid:gid is available via\n"
"    SO_PEERCRED and the uid:gid can be found in the set of users known\n"
"    to the Directory Server then that connection will be bound as that\n"
"    user.\n"
"\n"
"  * Otherwise an anonymous bind will occur.\n"
"\n"
"memcached UNIX socket behavior is as follows:\n"
"\n"
"  * memcached can be invoked with a user argument, no group may be\n"
"    specified. The effective uid is the uid of the user argument and\n"
"    the effective gid is the primary group of the user, let's call\n"
"    this euid:egid\n"
"\n"
"  * The socket ownership is: euid:egid\n"
"\n"
"  * The socket permissions are 0700 by default, but this can be\n"
"    modified by the -a mask command line arg which sets the umask\n"
"    (defaults to 0700).\n"
"\n"
"Overview of authentication in IPA\n"
"=================================\n"
"\n"
"This describes how we currently authenticate and how we plan to\n"
"improve authentication performance. First some definitions.\n"
"\n"
"There are 4 major players:\n"
"\n"
"  1. client\n"
"  2. mod_auth_kerb (in Apache process)\n"
"  3. wsgi handler (in IPA wsgi python process)\n"
"  4. ds (directory server)\n"
"\n"
"There are several resources:\n"
"\n"
"  1. /ipa/ui (unprotected, web UI static resources)\n"
"  2. /ipa/xml (protected, xmlrpc RPC used by command line clients)\n"
"  3. /ipa/json (protected, json RPC used by javascript in web UI)\n"
"  4. ds (protected, wsgi acts as proxy, our LDAP server)\n"
"\n"
"Current Model\n"
"-------------\n"
"\n"
"This describes how things work in our current system for the web UI.\n"
"\n"
"  1. Client requests /ipa/ui, this is unprotected, is static and\n"
"     contains no sensitive information. Apache replies with html and\n"
"     javascript. The javascript requests /ipa/json.\n"
"\n"
"  2. Client sends post to /ipa/json.\n"
"\n"
"  3. mod_auth_kerb is configured to protect /ipa/json, replies 401\n"
"     authenticate negotiate.\n"
"\n"
"  4. Client resends with credentials\n"
"\n"
"  5. mod_auth_kerb validates credentials\n"
"\n"
"     a. if invalid replies 403 access denied (stops here)\n"
"\n"
"     b. if valid creates temporary ccache, adds KRB5CCNAME to request\n"
"        headers\n"
"\n"
"  6. Request passed to wsgi handler\n"
"\n"
"     a. validates request, KRB5CCNAME must be present, referrer, etc.\n"
"\n"
"     b. ccache saved and used to bind to ds\n"
"\n"
"     c. routes to specified RPC handler.\n"
"\n"
"  7. wsgi handler replies to client\n"
"\n"
"Proposed new session based optimization\n"
"---------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"The round trip negotiate and credential validation in steps 3,4,5 is\n"
"expensive. This can be avoided if we can cache the client\n"
"credentials. With client sessions we can store the client credentials\n"
"in the session bound to the client.\n"
"\n"
"A few notes about the session implementation.\n"
"\n"
"  * based on session cookies, cookies must be enabled\n"
"\n"
"  * session cookie is secure, only passed on secure connections, only\n"
"    passed to our URL resource, never visible to client javascript\n"
"    etc.\n"
"\n"
"  * session cookie has a session id which is used by wsgi handler to\n"
"    retrieve client session data from shared multi-process cache.\n"
"\n"
"Changes to Apache's resource protection\n"
"---------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"  * /ipa/json is no longer protected by mod_auth_kerb. This is\n"
"    necessary to avoid the negotiate expense in steps 3,4,5\n"
"    above. Instead the /ipa/json resource will be protected in our wsgi\n"
"    handler via the session cookie.\n"
"\n"
"  * A new protected URI is introduced, /ipa/login. This resource\n"
"    does no serve any data, it is used exclusively for authentication.\n"
"\n"
"The new sequence is:\n"
"\n"
"  1. Client requests /ipa/ui, this is unprotected. Apache replies with\n"
"     html and javascript. The javascript requests /ipa/json.\n"
"\n"
"  2. Client sends post to /ipa/json, which is unprotected.\n"
"\n"
"  3. wsgi handler obtains session data from session cookie.\n"
"\n"
"     a. if ccache is present in session data and is valid\n"
"\n"
"        - request is further validated\n"
"\n"
"        - ccache is established for bind to ds\n"
"\n"
"        - request is routed to RPC handler\n"
"\n"
"        - wsgi handler eventually replies to client\n"
"\n"
"     b. if ccache is not present or not valid processing continues ...\n"
"\n"
"  4. wsgi handler replies with 401 Unauthorized\n"
"\n"
"  5. client sends request to /ipa/login to obtain session credentials\n"
"\n"
"  6. mod_auth_kerb replies 401 negotiate on /ipa/login\n"
"\n"
"  7. client sends credentials to /ipa/login\n"
"\n"
"  8. mod_auth_kerb validates credentials\n"
"\n"
"     a. if valid\n"
"\n"
"        - mod_auth_kerb permits access to /ipa/login. wsgi handler is\n"
"          invoked and does the following:\n"
"\n"
"          * establishes session for client\n"
"\n"
"          * retrieves the ccache from KRB5CCNAME and stores it\n"
"\n"
"     a. if invalid\n"
"\n"
"        - mod_auth_kerb sends 403 access denied (processing stops)\n"
"\n"
"  9. client now posts the same data again to /ipa/json including\n"
"     session cookie. Processing repeats starting at step 2 and since\n"
"     the session data now contains a valid ccache step 3a executes, a\n"
"     successful reply is sent to client.\n"
"\n"
"Command line client using xmlrpc\n"
"--------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"The above describes the web UI utilizing the json RPC mechanism. The\n"
"IPA command line tools utilize a xmlrpc RPC mechanism on the same\n"
"HTTP server. Access to the xmlrpc is via the /ipa/xml URI. The json\n"
"and xmlrpc API's are the same, they differ only on how their procedure\n"
"calls are marshalled and unmarshalled.\n"
"\n"
"Under the new scheme /ipa/xml will continue to be Kerberos protected\n"
"at all times. Apache's mod_auth_kerb will continue to require the\n"
"client provides valid Kerberos credentials.\n"
"\n"
"When the WSGI handler routes to /ipa/xml the Kerberos credentials will\n"
"be extracted from the KRB5CCNAME environment variable as provided by\n"
"mod_auth_kerb. Everything else remains the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Sesiju atbalsts IPA\n"
"John Dennis <jdennis@redhat.com>\n"
"\n"
"Mērķi\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Nodrošināt katra lietotāja sesijas datu kešošanu, kas saglabājas starp\n"
"pieprasījumiem. Vēlamās iespējas:\n"
"\n"
"* Tīri integrējas ar minimālu ietekmi uz esošo infrastruktūru.\n"
"\n"
"* Nodrošina maksimālu drošību, līdzsvarotu ar reālās dzīves veiktspējas\n"
"  prasībām.\n"
"\n"
"* Sesijām jābūt atsaucamām (iztīrāmām).\n"
"\n"
"* Jābūt elastīgam un izstrādātājiem viegli lietojamam.\n"
"\n"
"* Jāizmanto esošās tehnoloģijas un kods maksimāli iespējamā apjomā, lai\n"
"  izvairītos no atkārtotas izgudrošanas, pārmērīga realizācijas laika un\n"
"  gūtu labumu no praksē pārbaudītu komponentu robustuma, ko atvērtā\n"
"  pirmkoda kopiena plaši koplieto.\n"
"\n"
"* Jāatbalsta vairāki neatkarīgi procesi, kas koplieto sesijas\n"
"  datus.\n"
"\n"
"* Sistēmai jādarbojas pareizi neatkarīgi no tā, vai sesijas dati ir "
"pieejami.\n"
"\n"
"* Jābūt augstai veiktspējai.\n"
"\n"
"* Nevajadzētu būt piesaistītam konkrētiem tīmekļa serveriem vai pārlūkiem.\n"
"  Jāintegrējas ar mūsu izvēlēto WSGI modeli.\n"
"\n"
"Problēmas\n"
"=========\n"
"\n"
"Sīkdatnes\n"
"---------\n"
"\n"
"Lielākā daļa sesiju realizāciju balstās uz sīkdatņu lietošanu. Sīkdatnēm\n"
"ir dažas raksturīgas problēmas.\n"
"\n"
"* Lietotājam ir iespēja atspējot sīkdatnes.\n"
"\n"
"* Lietotāja glabātie sīkdatņu dati nav droši. To var mazināt, iestatot\n"
"  karogus, kas norāda, ka sīkdatne lietojama tikai ar SSL aizsargātiem\n"
"  HTTP savienojumiem uz konkrētiem tīmekļa resursiem, un iestatot, lai\n"
"  sīkdatnes derīgums beigtos līdz ar sesiju. Lielākā daļa mūsdienu\n"
"  pārlūku to ievēro.\n"
"\n"
"Kur glabāt sesijas datus?\n"
"-------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Sesijas datus var glabāt vai nu klientā, vai serverī. Sesijas datu\n"
"glabāšana klientā atrisina sesijas datu pieejamības problēmu, kad\n"
"pieprasījumus apkalpo neatkarīgi tīmekļa serveri, jo sesijas dati\n"
"ceļo kopā ar pieprasījumu. Taču ir datu izmēra ierobežojumi. Sesijas datu\n"
"glabāšana klientā arī atklāj sensitīvus datus, bet to var mazināt,\n"
"šifrējot sesijas datus tā, lai tos varētu atšifrēt tikai serveris.\n"
"\n"
"Ierastāka pieeja ir piesaistīt sesijas datus unikālam nosaukumam —\n"
"sesijas ID. Sesijas ID tiek nosūtīts klientam, un serverī sesijas dati\n"
"tiek sasaistīti ar sesijas ID asociatīvā datu krātuvē. Saņemot\n"
"pieprasījumu, serveris iegūst sesijas datus pēc sesijas ID. Tas novērš\n"
"sensitīvu sesijas datu atklāšanu klientā, kā arī datu izmēra\n"
"ierobežojumus. Taču tas rada sesijas datu pieejamības problēmu, kad\n"
"pieprasījumus apkalpo vairāk nekā viens servera process.\n"
"\n"
"Sesijas datu pieejamība vairākiem procesiem\n"
"-------------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Apache (un citi tīmekļa serveri) pieprasījumu paralēlai apstrādei\n"
"dakšo bērnprocesus. Turklāt tīmekļa serverus var izvietot fermā, kur\n"
"pieprasījumi tiek līdzsvaroti pēc kārtas starp dažādiem mezgliem. Abos\n"
"gadījumos sesijas datus nevar glabāt servera procesa atmiņā, jo tie\n"
"nav pieejami citiem procesiem — ne galvenā servera procesa radniecīgajiem\n"
"bērniem, ne servera procesiem atsevišķos mezglos.\n"
"\n"
"Parasti to risina, glabājot sesijas datus SQL datubāzē. Kad servera\n"
"process saņem pieprasījumu, kura sīkdatnes datos ir sesijas ID, sesijas\n"
"ID tiek lietots SQL vaicājuma izpildei, un iegūtie dati tiek pievienoti\n"
"pieprasījumam, tam virzoties pa pieprasījumu apstrādes konveijeru. Tas,\n"
"protams, rada saskaņotības problēmas.\n"
"\n"
"IPA gadījumā SQL datubāzes atkarības ieviešana nav vēlama, un no tās\n"
"jāizvairās.\n"
"\n"
"Neatkarīgi procesi var koplietot sesijas datus arī, glabājot sesijas\n"
"datus failos.\n"
"\n"
"Alternatīvs risinājums, kas pēdējā laikā guvis ievērojamu popularitāti,\n"
"ir ātra, uz atmiņu balstīta kešošanas servera lietošana. Dati tiek\n"
"glabāti viena procesa atmiņā, un tos var vaicāt un iestatīt ar vieglu\n"
"protokolu, lietojot standarta ligzdu mehānismus; memcached ir viens\n"
"piemērs. Tipisks lietojums ir SQL vaicājumu optimizēšana, glabājot SQL\n"
"rezultātu koplietotas atmiņas kešatmiņā un izvairoties no dārgākas SQL\n"
"operācijas. Bet atmiņas kešatmiņai ir izteiktas priekšrocības arī\n"
"situācijās bez SQL.\n"
"\n"
"Iespējamās realizācijas lietošanai IPA\n"
"======================================\n"
"\n"
"Apache sesijas\n"
"--------------\n"
"\n"
"Apache 2.3 sesiju atbalstu ir realizējis ar šiem moduļiem:\n"
"\n"
"  mod_session\n"
"    Vispārējs sesiju atbalsts, balstīts uz sīkdatnēm.\n"
"\n"
"    Skatiet: http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.3/mod/mod_session.html\n"
"\n"
"  mod_session_cookie\n"
"    Glabā sesijas datus klientā.\n"
"\n"
"    Skatiet: http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.3/mod/mod_session_cookie.html\n"
"\n"
"  mod_session_crypto\n"
"    Drošības nolūkā šifrē sesijas datus. Šifrēšanas atslēga ir koplietots\n"
"    konfigurācijas parametrs, kas redzams visiem Apache procesiem un tiek\n"
"    glabāts konfigurācijas failā.\n"
"\n"
"    Skatiet: http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.3/mod/mod_session_crypto.html\n"
"\n"
"  mod_session_dbd\n"
"    Glabā sesijas datus SQL datubāzē, ļaujot vairākiem procesiem\n"
"    piekļūt tiem pašiem sesijas datiem un tos koplietot.\n"
"\n"
"    Skatiet: http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.3/mod/mod_session_dbd.html\n"
"\n"
"Problēmas ar Apache sesijām\n"
"~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"\n"
"Lai gan Apache ir realizējis vispārīgu sesiju atbalstu un Apache ir mūsu\n"
"vēlamais tīmekļa serveris, tas tomēr rada problēmas IPA.\n"
"\n"
"  * Sesiju atbalsts pieejams tikai httpd >= 2.3, kas šī raksta tapšanas\n"
"    laikā augšteces pieejams tikai kā beta laidiens. Pašlaik\n"
"    piegādājam tikai httpd 2.2, un tas pats attiecas uz citām "
"distribūcijām.\n"
"\n"
"  * Sesiju moduļus httpd 2.2 vidēs varētu iepakot un piegādāt kā pagaidu\n"
"    pakotni. Bet tam ir šādas sekas:\n"
"\n"
"      - Kods jāpārnes uz vecāku versiju. Moduļu API starp httpd 2.2 un 2.3\n"
"        ir nedaudz mainījies. Pārnešana nav pārāk sarežģīta, un\n"
"        koncepcijas pierādījums ir realizēts.\n"
"\n"
"      - Tad mums būtu jāiepako un jāuztur īpaša gadījuma Apache pakotne.\n"
"        Tas ir uzturēšanas slogs, kā arī distribūcijas pakošanas slogs.\n"
"        No abiem, ja iespējams, vislabāk būtu izvairīties.\n"
"\n"
"  * Apache sesiju moduļi ir veidoti tā, ka tos var manipulēt tikai citi\n"
"    Apache moduļi. Sesijas datu patērētāju spēja kontrolēt sesijas\n"
"    datus ir vienkāršota, ierobežota un statiska laikā, kad pieprasījums\n"
"    tiek apstrādāts. Pieprasījumu apstrādātāji, kas nav iebūvēti Apache\n"
"    moduļi (piem., IPA caur WSGI), var aplūkot sesijas datus tikai\n"
"    caur pieprasījuma galvenēm un atiestatīt tos atbildes galvenēs.\n"
"\n"
"  * Koplietotie sesijas dati pieejami tikai caur SQL.\n"
"\n"
"Taču 2.3 Apache sesiju moduļu lietošana dotu mums robustu sesiju\n"
"atbalstu, realizētu C valodā un balstītu uz plaši lietotām\n"
"standartizētām Apache saskarnēm.\n"
"\n"
"Python tīmekļa ietvari\n"
"----------------------\n"
"\n"
"Praktiski visi Python tīmekļa ietvari atbalsta uz sīkdatnēm balstītas\n"
"sesijas, piem., Django, Twisted, Zope, Turbogears u.c. Jau agri IPA\n"
"nolēmām izvairīties no šo ietvaru lietošanas. Mēģinājums ievilkt tikai\n"
"vienu šo ietvaru daļu tikai sesiju atbalsta dēļ būtu problemātisks,\n"
"jo kods ārpus sava ietvara nedarbojas.\n"
"\n"
"IPA realizētās sesijas\n"
"----------------------\n"
"\n"
"Sākotnēji tika uzskatīts, ka vismazāko pūļu ceļš ir izmantot esošu\n"
"sesiju atbalstu, visticamāk, to, ko nodrošinātu Apache. Taču iebūvētajā\n"
"Python un citās standarta pakotnēs ir pietiekami daudz pamata moduļu\n"
"komponentu, lai ar mērenām realizācijas pūlēm vajadzētu būt iespējamam\n"
"nodrošināt sesiju atbalstu, kas atbilst iepriekš minētajiem mērķiem.\n"
"Tā kā izmantojam esošus komponentus, realizācijas grūtības pārņem citi\n"
"komponenti, kas jau pārbaudīti praksē un kam ir kopienas atbalsts. Tā\n"
"ir gudra stratēģija.\n"
"\n"
"Ierosinātais risinājums\n"
"=======================\n"
"\n"
"Mūsu saskarne ar tīmekļa serveri ir caur WSGI, kas katram pieprasījumam\n"
"izsauc atpakaļizsaukumu, nododot mums pieprasījuma vides kontekstu. Šajā\n"
"apspriedē WSGI atpakaļizsaukumu sauksim par \"application()\" — WSGI\n"
"terminoloģijā ierastu nosaukumu.\n"
"\n"
"Koplietotos sesijas datus apstrādās memcached. Katrā servera mezglā\n"
"izveidosim vienu memcached instanci, kas paredzēta tikai IPA.\n"
"Saziņa ar memcached notiks caur UNIX ligzdu, kas atrodas failu sistēmā\n"
"zem /var/run/ipa_memcached. To aizsargās failu atļaujas un pēc izvēles\n"
"SELinux politika.\n"
"\n"
"Funkcijā application() pārbaudām pieprasījuma sīkdatnes, un, ja ir IPA\n"
"sesijas sīkdatne ar sesijas ID, iegūstam sesijas datus no savas\n"
"memcached instances.\n"
"\n"
"Sesijas dati būs Python dict. IPA komponenti lasīs vai rakstīs savu\n"
"sesijas informāciju, lietojot iepriekš saskaņotu nosaukumu (t.i.,\n"
"atslēgu) dict. Tā ir ļoti elastīga sistēma, un tā saskan ar to, kā mēs\n"
"nododam datus lielākajā daļā IPA.\n"
"\n"
"Ja sesijas dati nav pieejami, tiks izveidots tukšs sesijas datu\n"
"dict.\n"
"\n"
"Kā šie sesijas dati ceļo kopā ar pieprasījumu pa IPA konveijeru? IPA\n"
"mēs lietojam HTTP pieprasījumu/atbildi, lai realizētu RPC. Funkcijā\n"
"application() pārveidojam pieprasījumu par procedūras izsaukumu, nododot\n"
"tam no HTTP pieprasījuma atvasinātus argumentus. Nodotie parametri ir\n"
"specifiski izsauktajai RPC metodei. Konteksts, kurā RPC izsaukums tiek\n"
"izpildīts, netiek nodots kā RPC parametrs.\n"
"\n"
"Kā kontekstuālā informācija, piemēram, sesijas dati, tiktu piesaistīta\n"
"pieprasījumam un līdz ar to RPC izsaukumam?\n"
"\n"
"IPA, kad no pieprasījuma tiek sagatavots RPC izsaukums, mēs zinām, ka\n"
"to vienmēr secīgi apstrādās tikai viens Python pavediens. Katram\n"
"pavedienam tiek piešķirts pavedienlokāls dict ar nosaukumu \"context\".\n"
"Konteksta dict tiek iztīrīts starp pieprasījumiem (t.i., RPC metožu\n"
"izsaukumiem). Katra pavediena konteksta dict tiek aizpildīts pieprasījuma\n"
"dzīves laikā un tiek lietots kā pieprasījumam unikāla globāla datu\n"
"struktūra, no kuras dažādi IPA komponenti var lasīt un kurā rakstīt ar\n"
"pārliecību, ka dati ir unikāli pašreizējam pieprasījumam un/vai metodes\n"
"izsaukumam.\n"
"\n"
"Sesijas datu dict tiks ierakstīts konteksta dict ar atslēgu session,\n"
"pirms RPC metode sāk izpildi. Tādējādi jebkurš IPA komponents var lasīt\n"
"un rakstīt sesijas datus, piekļūstot\n"
"``context.session``.\n"
"\n"
"Kad RPC metode beidz izpildi, pieprasījumam/metodei piesaistītie sesijas\n"
"dati tiek iegūti no konteksta un ierakstīti atpakaļ memcached\n"
"instancē. Sesijas ID tiek iestatīts klientam nosūtītajā atbildē\n"
"galvenē ``Set-Cookie`` kopā ar karogiem, kas kontrolē tā\n"
"lietošanu.\n"
"\n"
"Problēmas un detaļas\n"
"--------------------\n"
"\n"
"IPA kods nevar paļauties uz sesijas datu esamību, taču tam vienmēr\n"
"jāatjaunina sesijas dati cerībā, ka tie nākotnē būs pieejami. Sesijas\n"
"dati var nebūt pieejami, jo:\n"
"\n"
"  * Šis ir pirmais lietotāja pieprasījums, un sesijas dati vēl nav\n"
"    izveidoti.\n"
"\n"
"  * Lietotājam var būt atspējotas sīkdatnes.\n"
"\n"
"  * Sesijas dati var būt iztīrīti. memcached darbojas ar fiksētu\n"
"    atmiņas piešķīrumu un iztīrīs ierakstus pēc LRU principa; kā\n"
"    jebkurai kešatmiņai, saglabāšanās nav garantēta.\n"
"\n"
"    Mēs varam arī būt apzināti likuši beigties sesijas datu derīgumam vai\n"
"    izdzēsuši tos, skatiet tālāk.\n"
"\n"
"Sīkdatņu apstrāde tiek veikta ar standarta Python moduli Cookie.\n"
"\n"
"Sesiju sīkdatnes tiks iestatītas tā, lai tās saglabātos tikai tik ilgi,\n"
"kamēr pārlūkā sesija ir atvērta. Tās tiks atzīmētas, lai pārlūks sesijas\n"
"ID atgrieztu tikai SSL aizsargātos HTTP pieprasījumos. Tās nebūs redzamas\n"
"Javascript pārlūkā.\n"
"\n"
"Sesiju ID tiks veidoti no 48 bitiem nejaušu datu un pārvērsti 12\n"
"heksadecimālos ciparos. Jaunģenerētie sesiju ID tiks pārbaudīti, vai\n"
"tādi jau nepastāv, lai apstrādātu maz ticamo gadījumu, kad nejaušais\n"
"skaitlis atkārtojas.\n"
"\n"
"memcached veiktspēja būs ievērojami augstāka nekā SQL vai failu\n"
"krātuves risinājumam. Saziņa faktiski notiek caur kanālu\n"
"(UNIX ligzdu), lietojot ļoti vienkāršu protokolu, un dati pilnībā\n"
"glabājas procesa atmiņā. memcached arī viegli mērogojas — ir viegli\n"
"pievienot vairāk memcached procesu un sadalīt slodzi starp tiem.\n"
"Pašlaik neparedzam, ka tas būs vajadzīgs.\n"
"\n"
"Ļoti jauka Python moduļa memcached iespēja ir tā, ka, ierakstot datu\n"
"vienumu kešatmiņā, tas tiek darīts ar standarta Python pickling\n"
"(pickling ir standarta Python mehānisms Python objektu serializēšanai un\n"
"deserializēšanai). Pieņemam konvenciju, ka kešatmiņā rakstītais objekts\n"
"būs dict, lai atbilstu mūsu iekšējām datu apstrādes konvencijām.\n"
"Pickling kods rekursīvi apstrādās dict ligzdotos objektus. Tādējādi\n"
"iegūstam lielu elastību, lietojot standarta Python datu struktūras\n"
"sesijas datu glabāšanai un iegūšanai, bez nepieciešamības rakstīt un\n"
"atkļūdot kodu datu serializēšanai un deserializēšanai, ja būtu lietots\n"
"kāds cits glabāšanas mehānisms. Tas ir būtisks realizācijas ieguvums.\n"
"Protams, lemjot, ko rakstīt sesiju kešatmiņā, jāievēro daži veselā\n"
"saprāta ierobežojumi, paturot prātā, ka dati tiek koplietoti starp\n"
"procesiem un tiem nevajadzētu būt pārmērīgi lieliem (konfigurējama\n"
"opcija)\n"
"\n"
"memcached ierakstiem var iestatīt derīguma beigas. Varam izvēlēties to\n"
"darīt, lai piespiestu periodiski atsvaidzināt sesijas datus. Piemēram,\n"
"varam vēlēties, lai klients periodiski uzrāda svaigus akreditācijas\n"
"datus, pat ja kešotie akreditācijas dati citādi vēl ir derīgi.\n"
"\n"
"Sesijas datus varam skaidri izdzēst, ja kāda iemesla dēļ uzskatām, ka\n"
"tie ir novecojuši, nederīgi vai kompromitēti.\n"
"\n"
"memcached sniedz mums arī noteiktus līdzekļus sacensību stāvokļu\n"
"novēršanai starp dažādiem procesiem, kas izmanto kešatmiņu. Piemēram,\n"
"var pārbaudīt, vai ieraksts mainīts kopš pēdējās nolasīšanas, vai lietot\n"
"CAS (Check And Set) semantiku. Kas jāaizsargā kešatmiņas saskaņotības\n"
"ziņā, visticamāk, būs jānosaka, sesiju atbalstu izmantojot un\n"
"kešatmiņai pievienojot dažādus datu vienumus. Tas ir ļoti atkarīgs no\n"
"datiem un konteksta. Par laimi memcached operācijas ir\n"
"atomāras.\n"
"\n"
"memcached procesa kontrole\n"
"--------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Vajag mehānismu, lai startētu memcached procesu un aizsargātu to tā,\n"
"lai tam varētu piekļūt tikai IPA komponenti.\n"
"\n"
"Lai gan memcached tiek piegādāts gan ar initscript, gan systemd vienības\n"
"failiem, tie paredzēti vispārīgām instancēm. Mēs vēlamies memcached\n"
"instanci, kas paredzēta tikai IPA lietošanai. Lai to panāktu, mēs\n"
"instalētu systemd vienības failu vai SysV initscript IPA specifiskā\n"
"memcached pakalpojuma kontrolei. ipactl tiktu paplašināts, lai zinātu par\n"
"šo papildu pakalpojumu. systemd cgroup iespēja dotu mums papildu\n"
"mehānismus IPA memcached pakalpojuma integrēšanai lielākā IPA\n"
"procesu grupā.\n"
"\n"
"memcached datu aizsardzība tiktu veikta ar failu atļaujām (un\n"
"pēc izvēles SELinux politiku) UNIX domēna ligzdai. Lai gan jaunākās\n"
"memcached realizācijas atbalsta autentifikāciju caur SASL, tas\n"
"rada veiktspējas un sarežģītības slogu, kas nav attaisnojams, ja\n"
"kešatmiņa paredzēta tikai mūsu lietošanai un piekļuvi kontrolē OS\n"
"mehānismi.\n"
"\n"
"Ierasti dēmonus aizsargā, piešķirot dēmonam sistēmas uid un/vai\n"
"gid. root palaists dēmons atmet savas privilēģijas, pieņemot tam\n"
"piešķirto efektīvo uid:gid. Piekļuvi failu sistēmai kontrolē OS pēc\n"
"efektīvās identitātes, un SELinux politiku var veidot, balstoties uz\n"
"identitāti. Tādējādi memcached UNIX ligzda tiktu aizsargāta, piešķirot\n"
"tās īpašumtiesības konkrētam sistēmas lietotājam un/vai dalību\n"
"ierobežotā sistēmas grupā (pagaidām neņemot vērā\n"
"SELinux).\n"
"\n"
"Diemžēl pašlaik mums nav IPA sistēmas uid, ar kura identitāti\n"
"darbotos mūsu procesi, nedz arī IPA sistēmas grupas. IPA pārvalda\n"
"saistītu procesu (dēmonu) kopu, un vēsturiski katram ir piešķirts savs\n"
"uid. Kad šie nesaistītie procesi sazinās, tie savstarpēji autentificējas\n"
"ar citiem mehānismiem. Mums nav lielas vēstures koplietotu failu\n"
"sistēmas objektu lietošanā starp identitātēm. Kad tiek izveidoti failu\n"
"objekti, tiem parasti piešķir tā dēmona identitāti, kuram jāpiekļūst\n"
"objektam, un citi dēmoni tiem nepiekļūst, vai arī tiem ir root\n"
"identitāte.\n"
"\n"
"Kad mūsu WSGI lietotne darbojas Apache, tā darbojas kā WSGI\n"
"dēmons. Tas nozīmē, ka, Apache startējot, tas mums dakšo WSGI procesus,\n"
"un mēs esam neatkarīgi no citiem Apache procesiem. Kad WSGI darbojas\n"
"šajā režīmā, ir iespēja iestatīt mūs mitinošā WSGI procesa uid:gid,\n"
"taču pašlaik šo iespēju neizmantojam. WSGI var darbināt arī citos\n"
"režīmos; tikai dēmona režīmā uid:gid var iestatīt neatkarīgi no pārējā\n"
"Apache. Visus Apache startētos procesus var iestatīt uz kopīgu uid:gid,\n"
"kas norādīts globālajā Apache konfigurācijā; pēc noklusējuma tas ir\n"
"apache:apache. Tādējādi, kad mūsu IPA kods tiek izpildīts, tas darbojas\n"
"kā apache:apache.\n"
"\n"
"Lai aizsargātu savu memcached UNIX ligzdu, varam darīt vienu no divām "
"lietām:\n"
"\n"
"1. Piešķirt tās uid:gid kā apache:apache. Tas ierobežotu piekļuvi\n"
"   mūsu kešatmiņai tikai ar procesiem, kas darbojas zem httpd. Tas ir "
"zināmā\n"
"   mērā ierobežoti, bet tālu no ideāla. Jebkurš tīmekļa serverī\n"
"   darbināts kods potenciāli varētu piekļūt mūsu kešatmiņai. Ir grūti\n"
"   kontrolēt, ko tīmekļa serveris darbina, un administratori var neizprast\n"
"   sekas, konfigurējot httpd izsniegt vēl citas lietas bez IPA.\n"
"\n"
"2. Izveidot IPA specifisku uid:gid, piemēram, ipa:ipa. Tad konfigurējam\n"
"   savu WSGI lietotni darboties kā lietotājs un grupa ipa:ipa. Arī\n"
"   memcached instanci konfigurējam darboties kā lietotājs un grupa\n"
"   ipa:ipa. Šajā konfigurācijā esam pilnībā aizsargāti — tikai mūsu WSGI\n"
"   kods var lasīt un rakstīt mūsu memcached UNIX ligzdā.\n"
"\n"
"Taču, pārveidojot mūsu kodu darbībai kā kaut kas cits nekā apache:apache,\n"
"var rasties neparedzētas problēmas. Tam vajadzētu zināmu\n"
"izpēti un testēšanu.\n"
"\n"
"IPA ir atkarīgs no citiem sistēmas dēmoniem, konkrēti Directory\n"
"Server (ds) un Certificate Server (cs). Pašlaik ds konfigurējam\n"
"darboties zem lietotāja un grupas dirsrv:dirsrv — mūsu radītas\n"
"identitātes. cs ļaujam pēc noklusējuma lietot tā lietotāju un grupu\n"
"pkiuser:pkiuser. Vai šiem citiem sadarbības dēmoniem arī vajadzētu\n"
"darboties zem kopīgās lietotāja un grupas identitātes ipa:ipa? No pirmā\n"
"acu uzmetiena šķiet, ka būtu priekšrocība apvienot visas procesu\n"
"identitātes zem kopīgas IPA lietotāja un grupas identitātes. Taču šie\n"
"citi procesi nepaļaujas uz lietotāja un grupas atļaujām, strādājot ar\n"
"ārējiem aģentiem, procesiem u.c. Drīzāk tie veidoti kā patstāvīgi\n"
"tīkla pakalpojumi, kas savus klientus autentificē ar citiem\n"
"mehānismiem. Tie paļaujas uz lietotāja un grupas atļaujām savu failu\n"
"sistēmas objektu pārvaldībai. Ja kaut kādā veidā ipa lietotājs un/vai\n"
"grupa tiktu kompromitēti vai ļaunprātīgs kods kaut kā tiktu izpildīts\n"
"ar ipa identitāti, būtu priekšrocība, ja sadarbības procesi būtu\n"
"nodalīti zem savām identitātēm, nodrošinot vienu papildu\n"
"aizsardzības slāni. (Piezīme: šie sadarbības dēmoni var pat nebūt\n"
"izvietoti tajā pašā mezglā, un tādā gadījumā jautājums ir nebūtisks)\n"
"\n"
"UNIX ligzdas (ldapi) uzvedība ar Directory Server ir šāda:\n"
"\n"
"  * Ligzdas īpašumtiesības: root:root\n"
"\n"
"  * Ligzdas atļaujas: 0666\n"
"\n"
"  * Savienojoties caur ldapi, jāautentificējas tāpat kā parasti\n"
"    ar TCP ligzdu, izņemot ...\n"
"\n"
"  * Ja autobind ir iespējots un uid:gid ir pieejams caur\n"
"    SO_PEERCRED un uid:gid atrodams Directory Server zināmo lietotāju\n"
"    kopā, tad savienojums tiks piesaistīts kā šis\n"
"    lietotājs.\n"
"\n"
"  * Citādi notiks anonīma piesaiste.\n"
"\n"
"memcached UNIX ligzdas uzvedība ir šāda:\n"
"\n"
"  * memcached var izsaukt ar lietotāja argumentu, grupu norādīt\n"
"    nevar. Efektīvais uid ir lietotāja argumenta uid, un\n"
"    efektīvais gid ir lietotāja primārā grupa; sauksim\n"
"    tos par euid:egid\n"
"\n"
"  * Ligzdas īpašumtiesības: euid:egid\n"
"\n"
"  * Ligzdas atļaujas pēc noklusējuma ir 0700, bet tās var\n"
"    mainīt ar komandrindas argumentu -a mask, kas iestata umask\n"
"    (noklusējums 0700).\n"
"\n"
"Autentifikācijas pārskats IPA\n"
"=============================\n"
"\n"
"Šis apraksta, kā pašlaik autentificējam un kā plānojam\n"
"uzlabot autentifikācijas veiktspēju. Vispirms dažas definīcijas.\n"
"\n"
"Ir 4 galvenie dalībnieki:\n"
"\n"
"  1. klients\n"
"  2. mod_auth_kerb (Apache procesā)\n"
"  3. wsgi apstrādātājs (IPA wsgi python procesā)\n"
"  4. ds (direktoriju serveris)\n"
"\n"
"Ir vairāki resursi:\n"
"\n"
"  1. /ipa/ui (neaizsargāts, tīmekļa UI statiskie resursi)\n"
"  2. /ipa/xml (aizsargāts, xmlrpc RPC, ko lieto komandrindas klienti)\n"
"  3. /ipa/json (aizsargāts, json RPC, ko lieto javascript tīmekļa UI)\n"
"  4. ds (aizsargāts, wsgi darbojas kā starpniekserveris, mūsu LDAP serveris)"
"\n"
"\n"
"Pašreizējais modelis\n"
"--------------------\n"
"\n"
"Šis apraksta, kā lietas darbojas mūsu pašreizējā sistēmā tīmekļa UI.\n"
"\n"
"  1. Klients pieprasa /ipa/ui; tas ir neaizsargāts, statisks un\n"
"     nesatur sensitīvu informāciju. Apache atbild ar html un\n"
"     javascript. Javascript pieprasa /ipa/json.\n"
"\n"
"  2. Klients nosūta post uz /ipa/json.\n"
"\n"
"  3. mod_auth_kerb ir konfigurēts aizsargāt /ipa/json, atbild 401\n"
"     authenticate negotiate.\n"
"\n"
"  4. Klients nosūta atkārtoti ar akreditācijas datiem\n"
"\n"
"  5. mod_auth_kerb validē akreditācijas datus\n"
"\n"
"     a. ja nederīgi, atbild 403 access denied (te apstājas)\n"
"\n"
"     b. ja derīgi, izveido pagaidu ccache, pievieno KRB5CCNAME pieprasījuma\n"
"        galvenēm\n"
"\n"
"  6. Pieprasījums nodots wsgi apstrādātājam\n"
"\n"
"     a. validē pieprasījumu; jābūt KRB5CCNAME, referrer u.c.\n"
"\n"
"     b. ccache saglabāts un lietots piesaistei ds\n"
"\n"
"     c. maršrutē uz norādīto RPC apstrādātāju.\n"
"\n"
"  7. wsgi apstrādātājs atbild klientam\n"
"\n"
"Ierosinātā jaunā, uz sesijām balstītā optimizācija\n"
"--------------------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Negotiate apmaiņa un akreditācijas datu validēšana 3., 4., 5. solī ir\n"
"dārga. No tās var izvairīties, ja varam kešot klienta\n"
"akreditācijas datus. Ar klientu sesijām klienta akreditācijas datus\n"
"varam glabāt klientam piesaistītajā sesijā.\n"
"\n"
"Dažas piezīmes par sesiju realizāciju.\n"
"\n"
"  * balstīta uz sesiju sīkdatnēm, sīkdatnēm jābūt iespējotām\n"
"\n"
"  * sesijas sīkdatne ir droša, tiek nodota tikai drošos savienojumos, tikai\n"
"    mūsu URL resursam, nekad nav redzama klienta javascript\n"
"    u.c.\n"
"\n"
"  * sesijas sīkdatnē ir sesijas ID, ko wsgi apstrādātājs lieto, lai\n"
"    iegūtu klienta sesijas datus no koplietotas vairākprocesu kešatmiņas.\n"
"\n"
"Izmaiņas Apache resursu aizsardzībā\n"
"-----------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"  * /ipa/json vairs neaizsargā mod_auth_kerb. Tas ir\n"
"    nepieciešams, lai izvairītos no negotiate izmaksām iepriekšējos 3., 4., "
"5.\n"
"    solī. Tā vietā resursu /ipa/json aizsargās mūsu wsgi\n"
"    apstrādātājs ar sesijas sīkdatni.\n"
"\n"
"  * Tiek ieviests jauns aizsargāts URI — /ipa/login. Šis resurss\n"
"    neizsniedz nekādus datus, tas tiek lietots tikai autentifikācijai.\n"
"\n"
"Jaunā secība ir šāda:\n"
"\n"
"  1. Klients pieprasa /ipa/ui; tas ir neaizsargāts. Apache atbild ar\n"
"     html un javascript. Javascript pieprasa /ipa/json.\n"
"\n"
"  2. Klients nosūta post uz /ipa/json, kas ir neaizsargāts.\n"
"\n"
"  3. wsgi apstrādātājs iegūst sesijas datus no sesijas sīkdatnes.\n"
"\n"
"     a. ja sesijas datos ir ccache un tas ir derīgs\n"
"\n"
"        - pieprasījums tiek tālāk validēts\n"
"\n"
"        - tiek izveidots ccache piesaistei ds\n"
"\n"
"        - pieprasījums tiek maršrutēts uz RPC apstrādātāju\n"
"\n"
"        - wsgi apstrādātājs galu galā atbild klientam\n"
"\n"
"     b. ja ccache nav vai tas nav derīgs, apstrāde turpinās ...\n"
"\n"
"  4. wsgi apstrādātājs atbild ar 401 Unauthorized\n"
"\n"
"  5. klients nosūta pieprasījumu uz /ipa/login, lai iegūtu sesijas "
"akreditācijas datus\n"
"\n"
"  6. mod_auth_kerb atbild 401 negotiate uz /ipa/login\n"
"\n"
"  7. klients nosūta akreditācijas datus uz /ipa/login\n"
"\n"
"  8. mod_auth_kerb validē akreditācijas datus\n"
"\n"
"     a. ja derīgi\n"
"\n"
"        - mod_auth_kerb atļauj piekļuvi /ipa/login. Tiek izsaukts wsgi\n"
"          apstrādātājs, kas veic šo:\n"
"\n"
"          * izveido klientam sesiju\n"
"\n"
"          * iegūst ccache no KRB5CCNAME un saglabā to\n"
"\n"
"     a. ja nederīgi\n"
"\n"
"        - mod_auth_kerb nosūta 403 access denied (apstrāde apstājas)\n"
"\n"
"  9. klients tagad atkal nosūta tos pašus datus uz /ipa/json, iekļaujot\n"
"     sesijas sīkdatni. Apstrāde atkārtojas, sākot ar 2. soli, un, tā kā\n"
"     sesijas datos tagad ir derīgs ccache, tiek izpildīts 3.a solis, un\n"
"     klientam tiek nosūtīta sekmīga atbilde.\n"
"\n"
"Komandrindas klients, kas lieto xmlrpc\n"
"--------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Iepriekš aprakstīta tīmekļa UI, kas izmanto json RPC mehānismu. IPA\n"
"komandrindas rīki izmanto xmlrpc RPC mehānismu tajā pašā HTTP\n"
"serverī. Piekļuve xmlrpc notiek caur URI /ipa/xml. json un xmlrpc API\n"
"ir vienādi, tie atšķiras tikai ar to, kā to procedūru izsaukumi tiek\n"
"serializēti un deserializēti.\n"
"\n"
"Jaunajā shēmā /ipa/xml joprojām vienmēr būs aizsargāts ar Kerberos.\n"
"Apache mod_auth_kerb joprojām pieprasīs, lai klients uzrāda derīgus\n"
"Kerberos akreditācijas datus.\n"
"\n"
"Kad WSGI apstrādātājs maršrutē uz /ipa/xml, Kerberos akreditācijas dati\n"
"tiks iegūti no vides mainīgā KRB5CCNAME, ko nodrošina\n"
"mod_auth_kerb. Viss pārējais paliek nemainīgs.\n"

